# sgo.build (schema: see the sgola tree's core/sgo.build). wata-watch is an
# APP over core + json + wataclient + wataui: the standalone Apple Watch
# client (plan 0069). Its architecture is wata-ios's — a retained UIKit
# stage over the generated bindings — because watchOS's objc runtime has a
# working UIKit even though its headers mark UIView & co
# API_UNAVAILABLE(watchos). What differs is the ENTRY POINT: a watch app is
# started by WatchKit, so go-pkgs/watchshell owns WKApplicationMain and the
# scene-joined window in place of iosshell's UIApplicationMain.
mode app
emitname wata-watch
binname wata-watch
gomod watawatch
optreport
# The WatchKit shell (plan 0069) and the glue under the stage. iosui is
# REUSED UNCHANGED from the phone — it is libdispatch, libobjc and
# CoreGraphics, none of which is iOS-specific. Both ride appleptt (the
# generated uikit bindings), which needs its OWN godep line: a `replace` in
# a dependency's go.mod is ignored once the emitted app is the main module.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/watchshell go-pkgs/watchshell
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/iosui go-pkgs/iosui
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/appleptt go-pkgs/appleptt
# The audio backend, unchanged from the phone: AudioToolbox + AVFAudio over
# purego. Its session_ios.go is //go:build ios and the watch rides GOOS=ios,
# so the AVAudioSession work comes along. Probed on the watch simulator
# before this line was added — engine, playback, microphone and both codec
# ends all work (plan 0069's stage 3 section).
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/macaudio go-pkgs/macaudio
# the timeout-carrying http.Client constructor — the net/http facade binds the
# Client type, not its fields (RETIRE-HTTPC-SHIM retires this once the ruled
# timeout members land upstream)
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/httpc go-pkgs/httpc
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/irohnet go-pkgs/irohnet
